1
00:00:05,867 --> 00:00:07,407
(Leonard:)So, what's going on with Raj?

2
00:00:07,618 --> 00:00:10,368
(Howard:)Well, the good news
is he has no problem...

3
00:00:10,538 --> 00:00:12,538
...with my mother's tur-briska-fil.

4
00:00:12,707 --> 00:00:15,547
(Penny:)Hard to believe, but go on.

5
00:00:15,710 --> 00:00:18,340
(Howard:)The bad news
is he says he's getting deported.

6
00:00:18,504 --> 00:00:20,334
(Leonard:)What do you mean
he's getting deported?

7
00:00:20,506 --> 00:00:24,386
I believe it means the U.S. government
is going to expel him from the country.

8
00:00:24,552 --> 00:00:28,852
He could return to India, immigrate to
another country willing to accept him...

9
00:00:29,015 --> 00:00:31,725
(Sheldon:)...or wander the high seas
as a stateless pirate.

10
00:00:35,062 --> 00:00:37,192
(Sheldon:)Personally, I'd choose pirate.

11
00:00:38,733 --> 00:00:41,483
(Howard:)Penny, would you mind stepping outside
so we can speak to him?

12
00:00:41,652 --> 00:00:45,742
(Penny:)Ugh. Fine, but the man really needs to work
on his girl issues.

13
00:00:45,907 --> 00:00:48,037
(Sheldon:)Another reason
to consider a life of piracy.

14
00:00:48,201 --> 00:00:51,081
(Sheldon:)Even today, I understand
that's an all-male profession.

15
00:00:53,456 --> 00:00:55,746
(Howard:)Okay, she's gone.

16
00:00:59,795 --> 00:01:03,025
(Raj:)Sorry I lost my cool.

